cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  maniMon: a workstation monitor with persistent statistics
  and honest per-run cost accounting
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thatte
    given-names: Manish Jagdish
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8050-1242"
    affiliation: maniTLab, Nashik, Maharashtra, India
    email: manish@manitlab.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/manishthatte/maniMon"
url: "https://www.manitlab.org"
abstract: >-
  A Linux workstation monitor for machines that run long jobs.
  It reads sensors most monitors do not — the amdgpu gpu_metrics
  binary sysfs structure, the BMC over IPMI, SMART, ECC counters
  and the DIMM channel inventory — and keeps the history in a
  multi-resolution store rather than in per-process ring buffers
  that vanish on restart. Per-run accounting separates quantities
  measured per process, which are genuinely attributable, from
  machine-wide quantities such as GPU power, which are reported
  with their observed concurrency rather than divided between
  overlapping runs.
keywords:
  - system monitoring
  - amdgpu
  - IPMI
  - SMART
  - energy accounting
  - time series
  - Linux
